{"cluster_id": "C-1070", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-070"], "canonical_claim": "The `RefTableState` closed-class optimization design lists three residual risks: E3's overlay-level transaction layer moves the strong-exception-safety guarantee into new code and needs an explicit test that state is byte-for-byte unchanged after a throwing transaction; E4's flat-vector base has different iterator-invalidation rules than the old node-based map, so the closed class's read API must not leak the old iterator-stability promises; and `cas-gc-rebuild` is a shared branch worked concurrently by another session, requiring commit discipline (verify `HEAD` after commit, one ninja at a time, never rebase/amend).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments-design.md#risks"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1071", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-035"], "canonical_claim": "The heart conjunct of the Apalache inductive invariant, `InflightCurrentUnreferenced` (a delete message in flight for a still-current token implies no folded root edge and no unfolded add past the cursor), was proven irredundant by a negative control; dropping the `W-REVALIDATE` re-observation conjunct from `WPublish` produces a counterexample breaking `NoDangle`, machine-checking the F1 re-observation requirement.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#L157-L164"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1072", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-073"], "canonical_claim": "A TLA+ model is deleted, not kept, once keeping it would assert a guarantee the shipped code no longer makes; false comfort (an unfaithful model implying a safety property the code does not actually provide) is treated as worse than having no proof at all.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#patterns"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1073", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-106"], "canonical_claim": "dedupTrace independently traced the CAS write ordering in `ReplicatedMergeTreeSink`: the CAS commit (`renameParts`\u2192`stageManifest`, line 976) strictly precedes the atomic Keeper dedup-token multi-op (line 985), so a failed CAS write leaves no dedup token behind; this refuted the initially-suspected \"orphan-token\" mechanism for the R3 data-loss regression, though the acked-then-lost data loss itself remained confirmed via a separate mechanism.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-17-unattended-round2-part1.md#L33"]}
